>
> Interesting approach.  Just to clarify, do you mean that 
> it uses the existing code to decide what to display where,
> and then replaces the code that would print characters
> with alternate code that shows tiles, or does it actually
> call the existing character-printing code and capture and
> alter its output somehow, sort of like what Ebonhack does?

It uses the existing code to decide what to display where, and draws
text on most of the screen. The area where the map would be shown is
drawn with tiles instead. If a menu pops up above it, it's drawn with
text, with the tiles showing beneath. (Although there's currently a bug
in which the tiles behind the menu are scrolled to the wrong place,
that'll be fixed before release.)

